# XCU asa
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only the behaviours the page specifies are tested. The characters that
# stand for a page advance and a return to column 1 are implementation-defined,
# so those tests check that something other than a newline is written in the
# right place. The utility is shaded FR (Fortran runtime).

assertion  XCU.asa.001
anchor     utilities/asa.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       A line starting with a space is written without that character and otherwise unchanged.
test       t/001-space.sh

assertion  XCU.asa.002
anchor     utilities/asa.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       A line starting with 0 is preceded by a newline; only the first character of a line is the control character.
test       t/002-zero.sh

assertion  XCU.asa.003
anchor     utilities/asa.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       A line starting with 1 is preceded by one or more characters that advance to the next page.
test       t/003-one.sh

assertion  XCU.asa.004
anchor     utilities/asa.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       A line starting with + replaces the previous line's newline with characters that return to column 1; a + on the first line acts as a space.
test       t/004-plus.sh

assertion  XCU.asa.005
anchor     utilities/asa.html#OPERANDS/file
anchor     utilities/asa.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/asa.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       Files are written in order, standard input is used with no operand, and status is 0.
test       t/005-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.asa.006
anchor     utilities/asa.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       FR
since      1992
says       A file that cannot be read gives a nonzero status.
test       t/006-missing-file.sh
